You're right that a Gaussian model won't fit the data very well.  But I don't expect than anything will.  What you can see quite clearly in your plot is that a subset of the data appears to be coming from a totally different process.  Finding these clumps of data is one of the objectives we hope to achieve with our modeling efforts.

I can't comment on whether or not this is contributing to the convergence issues.  It sounds like a reasonable guess.

Thanks for taking a look!

Jonathon

