From ud4d87473a37ad6c0 at groups.google.com  Wed May 17 09:42:37 2017
From: ud4d87473a37ad6c0 at groups.google.com (Brian Lau)
Date: Wed, 17 May 2017 09:42:37 +0000
Subject: Re: Issue about saving warm-up samples in Matlab Stan
Message-ID: <NgRqOPI417I.TIhezwU0BAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <NgRqOPI417I.G53j_sM8AAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <NgRqOPI417I.EEB4Cv6uBwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com> <NgRqOPI417I.G53j_sM8AAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/NgRqOPI417I/m/TIhezwU0BAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Warmup samples are not saved by default. You can save the warmup samples using the 'inc_warmup' parameter. This is documented here:

https://github.com/brian-lau/MatlabStan/wiki/Extracting-samples

-b

